<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christmas Battles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1916–1917</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Christmas Battles were a Russian offensive against German positions near Riga in late December 1916 and January 1917, in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latvian-riflemen">Latvian Riflemen</a> units broke through the German lines in heavy winter fighting. The breakthrough was not exploited by the Russian command, and the Riflemen suffered several thousand casualties. The battles became a central episode in Latvian national memory and military tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christmas-battles.jpg" alt="Christmas Battles" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ziemassvetku_kaujas_1917.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
